From cd1efd9ce213489a2e8c78609c76cfc488d72293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 21:45:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/42] amdgpu: fix SMEM SBASE operand index and harden
 register reservation

Inst_SMEM::initOperandInfo registered the address base as the raw SBASE field
while execute() and generateDisassembly() both scale it by two, because SBASE
addresses an aligned SGPR pair with an implied LSB of 0. Dependency tracking
and register reads therefore observed the wrong physical registers; the live
gfx950 attention path faulted with a host-native scalar read at VA 0 because
the declared base resolved to s[8:9] instead of s[16:17].

Also make wave register reservation fail closed. A pool manager reports an
unsatisfiable request by returning an invalid start index without writing the
reserved size, which previously started a wave with a zero-length register
region and only failed later as an out-of-range register index. Release the
scalar region only when one was actually reserved, matching allocation.

Host-native vector and scalar memory faults now report the owning kernel, PC,
dispatch, instruction, kernarg head, and sourced scalar registers through one
generic helper so a fault names its cause instead of a bare address.

All changes are generic at the shared ISA, register-manager, and diagnostic
boundaries. No model, operator, kernel, shape, or address special case is
added.

